---
layout: base.njk
fieldPhotosPublic: true
permalink: /recommendations/
title: Initial Location Analysis | Rofo
description: Review an initial commercial location analysis with recommended starting areas, confidence signals, building examples, alternatives, and next steps.
eleventyComputed:
  canonical: "{{ metadata.siteUrl }}/recommendations/"
---

<section class="recommendations-page">
  <div class="recommendations-shell">
    <div class="breadcrumbs">
      <a href="/">Rofo</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span>Initial Location Analysis</span>
    </div>

    <section class="recommendations-hero">
      <div class="recommendations-hero__copy">
        <div class="eyebrow" data-recommendation-hero-badge>SAMPLE LOCATION ANALYSIS</div>
        <h1>Recommended starting locations for your search.</h1>
        <p class="lead" data-recommendation-hero-copy>
          Mission Bay is the strongest starting point for this profile. SoMa and the Financial District are useful comparisons before narrowing the search.
        </p>
        <dl class="recommendations-recap" aria-label="Search recap">
          <div>
            <dt>Location</dt>
            <dd data-recommendation-context-location data-recommendation-location>San Francisco</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Space</dt>
            <dd data-recommendation-context-space data-recommendation-space>Office</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Size</dt>
            <dd data-recommendation-context-size data-recommendation-size>2,500-5,000 sqft</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Intent</dt>
            <dd data-recommendation-context-intent>Compare with nearby markets</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="recommendation-context-card recommendation-memo-section" aria-labelledby="recommendation-context-heading" data-recommendation-context-card hidden>
      <div class="kicker" data-recommendation-context-kicker>Initial Analysis</div>
      <h2 id="recommendation-context-heading" data-recommendation-context-heading>Recommended starting point.</h2>
      <p class="recommendation-memo-lead" data-recommendation-context-copy>
        Mission Bay is the strongest starting point because it offers modern office inventory, strong transit access, and room for growth. SoMa and the Financial District are useful comparisons before narrowing the search to individual buildings.
      </p>
      <p data-recommendation-demo-detail>
        <a href="/example-location-brief/">View an Example Location Brief</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="recommendation-expert-guided" data-recommendation-expert-guided hidden>
      <div class="kicker">Expert Guided Analysis</div>
      <h2>This market needs expert review.</h2>
      <p>
        This profile has enough location, space type, and size context for a local market expert to review relevant options when you choose that next step.
      </p>
      <a class="recommendations-button" href="/find-locations/">Update Location Profile</a>
    </section>

    <section class="recommendations-section recommendation-memo-section" aria-labelledby="recommended-districts" data-recommendation-supported>
      <div class="recommendations-section__header">
        <div class="kicker" data-recommendation-section-kicker>Recommended Starting Path</div>
        <h2 id="recommended-districts" data-recommendation-section-heading>Start with the strongest fit, then pressure-test alternatives.</h2>
        <p>
          These are not live listing results. They are the first markets to evaluate before checking live availability, requesting introductions, or touring buildings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="recommendation-brief-grid" data-recommendation-brief-grid hidden>
        <section class="recommendation-brief-panel recommendation-brief-panel--path">
          <h3>Recommended starting point and why</h3>
          <div class="recommendation-market-path" data-recommendation-market-path></div>
        </section>

        <section class="recommendation-brief-panel">
          <h3>Why alternatives still matter</h3>
          <div class="recommendation-compare-list" data-recommendation-compare-with></div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="recommendations-section recommendation-memo-section" aria-labelledby="recommendation-rationale">
      <div class="recommendations-section__header">
        <div class="kicker">Decision Explanation</div>
        <h2 id="recommendation-rationale">Why this location, and why not the others first.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="recommendation-strategy" data-recommendation-strategy>
        Mission Bay offers the strongest combination of modern inventory, accessibility, amenity context, and future flexibility for this profile. SoMa and the Financial District should still be pressure-tested for pricing, commute patterns, and building availability.
      </p>
      <ul class="recommendation-evaluate-list recommendation-evaluate-list--memo" data-recommendation-evaluate-next>
        <li>Modern and flexible office inventory.</li>
        <li>Strong transit and talent access.</li>
        <li>Good fit for growth-stage companies.</li>
        <li>Useful comparison set before narrowing to individual buildings.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="recommendations-section recommendation-memo-section recommendation-primary-section" aria-labelledby="primary-market-deep-dive">
      <div class="recommendations-section__header">
        <div class="kicker">Primary Starting Point</div>
        <h2 id="primary-market-deep-dive" data-recommendation-primary-name>Mission Bay</h2>
        <p><span class="recommendation-status" data-recommendation-status>Recommended Starting Point</span></p>
      </div>
      <article class="recommendation-primary">
        <div class="recommendation-primary__body">
          <div class="recommendation-confidence" aria-label="Recommendation confidence summary">
            <span data-recommendation-fit-label><strong>96</strong> Match</span>
            <span data-recommendation-judgment-label>Strongly Recommended</span>
            <span data-recommendation-confidence-label>High Confidence</span>
          </div>
          <p class="recommendation-advice" data-recommendation-primary-advice>
            Mission Bay gives this search the best mix of modern office context, technology and life science adjacency, and room to compare buildings with larger, more current floor plates. It also keeps the search close to Caltrain-oriented access while staying connected to SoMa and the downtown core.
          </p>
          <p class="recommendation-note" data-recommendation-primary-note>
            Mission Bay should not be treated as the only answer. Use it as the baseline for quality, commute pattern, and expansion potential, then compare the alternatives against that standard.
          </p>
          <section class="recommendation-score-explainer" aria-labelledby="mission-bay-score">
            <h4 id="mission-bay-score" data-recommendation-explainer-heading>Why Mission Bay ranks first</h4>
            <div class="recommendation-advisor-grid">
              <section class="recommendation-advisor-panel">
                <h5>Why this location</h5>
                <ul>
                  <li data-recommendation-rationale-one>Requested office size aligns well with the type of modern buildings available to evaluate here.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-rationale-two>Mission Bay gives the search a strong technology and life science business context.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-rationale-three>Transit, Caltrain access, and regional commute routes make it a practical first market to test.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-rationale-four>Nearby amenities support teams that need a polished workplace environment.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-rationale-five>The district leaves room to compare multiple credible buildings before narrowing the search.</li>
                </ul>
              </section>

              <section class="recommendation-advisor-panel">
                <h5>Tradeoffs</h5>
                <ul class="recommendation-score-tradeoffs">
                  <li data-recommendation-tradeoff-one>Mission Bay can price at a premium versus nearby alternatives.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-tradeoff-two>It may not be the right first choice for a highly value-sensitive search.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-tradeoff-three>Some teams may prefer the older creative-office character found in SoMa.</li>
                </ul>
              </section>

              <section class="recommendation-advisor-panel">
                <h5>Best suited for</h5>
                <ul>
                  <li data-recommendation-fit-one>Technology companies that want modern office context.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-fit-two>Life science, healthcare, and research-adjacent teams.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-fit-three>Growth-stage companies that may need expansion flexibility.</li>
                  <li data-recommendation-fit-four>Teams that value UCSF, Caltrain, and waterfront-adjacent amenities.</li>
                </ul>
              </section>

              <section class="recommendation-advisor-panel recommendation-advisor-panel--confidence">
                <h5>What High Confidence means</h5>
                <p>
                  <span data-recommendation-confidence-copy>The initial inputs are strong enough to make Mission Bay a credible starting point: location, space type, and size all point toward a district with relevant building examples and clear nearby alternatives. A local market check would still confirm live options before any decision.</span>
                </p>
              </section>
            </div>
          </section>
          <div class="recommendation-actions">
            <a href="/commercial-real-estate/CA/san-francisco/mission-bay/" data-recommendation-primary-link>Explore District</a>
            <a href="/commercial-real-estate/CA/san-francisco/soma-vs-mission-bay/" data-recommendation-demo-detail>Compare to SoMa</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <aside class="recommendation-representative-buildings" aria-labelledby="primary-representative-buildings" data-recommendation-representative-buildings data-recommendation-demo-detail>
          <div class="recommendation-evidence__header">
            <div class="kicker">Representative examples</div>
            <h4 id="primary-representative-buildings" data-representative-buildings-heading>Representative buildings to understand this area</h4>
            <p data-representative-buildings-disclosure>These buildings are representative examples, not current availability. They help explain the kinds of commercial environments businesses commonly evaluate in this district.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="recommendation-building-list" data-representative-building-list>
            {% for building in recommendationRepresentativeBuildings.byDistrictSlug["mission-bay"].buildings %}
              {% if loop.index <= 3 %}
                <article class="recommendation-building-card recommendation-building-card--representative">
                  {% if building.image or building.fieldPhotoSubjectId %}
                    <img src="{{ building.image or '/images/placeholders/building-c.svg' }}" alt="{{ building.name }} in {{ building.city }}, {{ building.state }}" {% if building.fieldPhotoSubjectId %}data-building-photo-subject-id="{{ building.fieldPhotoSubjectId }}"{% endif %} loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                  {% endif %}
                  <div>
                    <span>{{ building.address }} · {{ building.buildingType }}</span>
                    <h5><a href="{{ building.canonicalUrl }}">View Building Brief: {{ building.name }}</a></h5>
                    <p><strong>Why it matters</strong>{{ building.representativeReason }}</p>
                    <p><strong>Best for</strong>{{ building.bestFitSummary }}</p>
                    <p><strong>Tradeoff</strong>{{ building.primaryTradeoff }}</p>
                  </div>
                </article>
              {% endif %}
            {% endfor %}
          </div>

          <div class="recommendation-live-market-panel" data-live-market-investigation-panel>
            <div>
              <h5>Ready to investigate the live market?</h5>
              <p>Representative buildings help explain the market. A Live Market Investigation looks at what is actually happening now.</p>
              <ul>
                <li>current availability</li>
                <li>future availability</li>
                <li>comparable buildings</li>
                <li>recent leasing activity</li>
                <li>market insight</li>
                <li>broker guidance when available</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="recommendation-live-market-panel__note">Availability and broker support depend on market coverage and current requirements.</p>
            </div>
            <a class="recommendations-button" href="#location-brief-contact" data-location-brief-review-trigger data-live-market-investigation-cta>Start Live Market Investigation</a>
          </div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="recommendations-section recommendation-memo-section" aria-labelledby="comparison-markets">
      <div class="recommendations-section__header">
        <div class="kicker">Comparison Markets</div>
        <h2 id="comparison-markets">Also worth comparing.</h2>
        <p>
          These markets should not carry the same weight as the primary recommendation. Use them to test commute, cost, building character, and market flexibility before narrowing to individual buildings.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="recommendation-compare-list recommendation-compare-list--memo" data-recommendation-compare-with-secondary hidden></div>
      <div class="recommendation-secondary-grid" aria-label="Alternative recommendations" data-recommendation-demo-detail>
        <article class="recommendation-card">
          <div class="recommendation-card__topline">
            <span class="recommendation-status">Strong Alternative</span>
          </div>
          <h3>SoMa</h3>
          <p class="recommendation-advice">
            SoMa is the strongest alternative if the search needs more building variety, a more central downtown position, or a creative office feel. It is worth comparing closely against Mission Bay because it can offer flexible formats while keeping access to downtown, Mission Bay, and transit-oriented corridors.
          </p>
          <div class="recommendation-actions">
            <a href="/commercial-real-estate/CA/san-francisco/soma/">Explore District</a>
            <a href="/commercial-real-estate/CA/san-francisco/soma-vs-mission-bay/">Compare to Mission Bay</a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="recommendation-card">
          <div class="recommendation-card__topline">
            <span class="recommendation-status">Worth Exploring</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Financial District</h3>
          <p class="recommendation-advice">
            The Financial District is worth exploring if client access, transit, and a more traditional office-core environment matter. It may be less aligned with a newer innovation-campus feel, but it can be a smart benchmark for pricing, commute convenience, and professional-service credibility.
          </p>
          <div class="recommendation-actions">
            <a href="/commercial-real-estate/CA/san-francisco/financial-district/">Explore District</a>
            <a href="/commercial-real-estate/CA/san-francisco/financial-district-vs-soma/">Compare to SoMa</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="location-brief-refinement" aria-labelledby="location-brief-refinement-heading" data-location-brief-refinement>
      <div class="location-brief-refinement__intro">
        <div class="kicker">Refine the analysis</div>
        <h2 id="location-brief-refinement-heading">Add detail when the first direction is visible.</h2>
        <p>Additional requirements can sharpen the market review after the recommended direction is visible.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="location-brief-refinement__grid">
        <section class="location-brief-refinement__panel" aria-labelledby="brief-feedback-heading">
          <h3 id="brief-feedback-heading">Does this direction feel right?</h3>
          <div class="location-brief-choice-list" data-location-brief-feedback>
            <button type="button" data-feedback-value="yes">Yes, this looks right</button>
            <button type="button" data-feedback-value="another_direction">Show me another direction</button>
            <button type="button" data-feedback-value="additional_requirements">I have additional requirements</button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="location-brief-refinement__panel" aria-labelledby="brief-priorities-heading">
          <h3 id="brief-priorities-heading">What matters most for this location?</h3>
          <p>Choose any priorities that should shape the expert review.</p>
          <div class="location-brief-priority-list" data-location-brief-priorities></div>
        </section>

        <section class="location-brief-refinement__panel" aria-labelledby="brief-questions-heading">
          <h3 id="brief-questions-heading">Questions to validate next</h3>
          <ul class="location-brief-question-list" data-location-brief-questions>
            <li>Current availability in the recommended market path.</li>
            <li>Asking rents, concessions, and lease structure.</li>
            <li>Comparable buildings and nearby alternatives.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="location-brief-refinement__panel" aria-labelledby="brief-notes-heading">
          <h3 id="brief-notes-heading">Additional notes</h3>
          <label class="location-brief-notes-label" for="location-brief-notes">Optional notes</label>
          <textarea id="location-brief-notes" data-location-brief-notes rows="4" placeholder="Example: We are growing quickly, parking is critical, or clients visit weekly."></textarea>
        </section>
      </div>

    </section>

    <form class="recommendations-cta location-brief-contact location-brief-contact--final" id="location-brief-contact" data-location-brief-contact aria-labelledby="market-investigation" method="post" action="/api/location-brief/submit">
      <div class="location-brief-contact__header">
        <div class="kicker" data-recommendation-cta-kicker>Optional Expert Review</div>
        <h2 id="market-investigation" data-recommendation-cta-heading>Request expert review when you are ready.</h2>
        <p data-recommendation-cta-copy>
          Share your profile only when you want expert follow-up on listings, comps, sublease options, incentives, and market guidance.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="recommendations-cta__panel">
        <h3>What an expert can help with</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Current availability</li>
          <li>Asking rents</li>
          <li>Landlord incentives</li>
          <li>Sublease opportunities</li>
          <li>Upcoming vacancies</li>
          <li>Off-market options</li>
          <li>Comparable buildings</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <section class="live-market-intake" aria-labelledby="live-market-intake-heading" data-live-market-investigation-intake hidden>
        <div class="live-market-intake__header">
          <div class="kicker">Live Market Investigation</div>
          <h3 id="live-market-intake-heading" data-live-market-intake-heading>Investigate this market</h3>
          <p data-live-market-intake-summary>Confirm what Rofo should investigate next. These are representative buildings, not confirmed availability.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="live-market-intake__context" aria-label="Recommendation context">
          <dl>
            <div>
              <dt>Recommended city</dt>
              <dd data-live-market-intake-city>To confirm</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>District</dt>
              <dd data-live-market-intake-district>To confirm</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Search profile</dt>
              <dd data-live-market-intake-profile>Profile details preserved</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <fieldset class="live-market-intake__fieldset" data-live-market-building-fieldset>
          <legend>Buildings to include</legend>
          <p>Keep the representative buildings Rofo should use as reference points. You can still ask Rofo to investigate the district even if no individual building remains selected.</p>
          <div class="live-market-building-options" data-live-market-building-options></div>
          <label class="live-market-check">
            <input type="checkbox" data-investigation-competitive-buildings checked>
            <span>Include other competitive buildings in this district</span>
          </label>
        </fieldset>

        <fieldset class="live-market-intake__fieldset">
          <legend>What should Rofo investigate?</legend>
          <p>Comp availability and quality vary by market. Select only what matters for the next review.</p>
          <div class="live-market-scope-grid" data-live-market-scope-options>
            <label class="live-market-check"><input type="checkbox" value="currentAvailability" checked> <span>Current availability</span></label>
            <label class="live-market-check"><input type="checkbox" value="futureAvailability" checked> <span>Future or upcoming availability</span></label>
            <label class="live-market-check"><input type="checkbox" value="comparableBuildings" checked> <span>Comparable buildings</span></label>
            <label class="live-market-check"><input type="checkbox" value="leasingActivity"> <span>Recent leasing activity or comps</span></label>
            <label class="live-market-check"><input type="checkbox" value="marketInsight"> <span>Market conditions and tenant considerations</span></label>
            <label class="live-market-check"><input type="checkbox" value="brokerGuidance"> <span>Broker guidance when available</span></label>
          </div>
        </fieldset>

        <div class="live-market-intake__grid">
          <section class="live-market-intake__fieldset" aria-labelledby="live-market-requirements-heading">
            <h4 id="live-market-requirements-heading">Requirements to confirm</h4>
            <dl class="live-market-requirements" data-live-market-requirements></dl>
            <label class="live-market-field">
              <span>Timing</span>
              <select data-live-market-timing>
                <option value="">Use profile timing if available</option>
                <option value="immediately">Immediately</option>
                <option value="within_3_months">Within 3 months</option>
                <option value="3_6_months">3-6 months</option>
                <option value="6_12_months">6-12 months</option>
                <option value="more_than_12_months">More than 12 months</option>
                <option value="exploring">Exploring with no fixed date</option>
              </select>
            </label>
          </section>

          <fieldset class="live-market-intake__fieldset">
            <legend>How should Rofo proceed?</legend>
            <div class="live-market-radio-list" data-live-market-broker-preference>
              <label class="live-market-check"><input type="radio" name="broker_preference" value="research_first" checked> <span>Research first; contact me with findings</span></label>
              <label class="live-market-check"><input type="radio" name="broker_preference" value="include_local_broker"> <span>Include local broker guidance when available</span></label>
              <label class="live-market-check"><input type="radio" name="broker_preference" value="already_working_with_broker"> <span>I am already working with a broker</span></label>
              <label class="live-market-check"><input type="radio" name="broker_preference" value="not_sure"> <span>Not sure yet</span></label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>
        </div>

        <label class="live-market-field live-market-field--notes">
          <span>Anything else Rofo should understand before investigating? <em>optional</em></span>
          <textarea data-live-market-notes rows="4" placeholder="Examples: exact streets, parking needs, expansion plans, current lease timing, infrastructure requirements, or building types to avoid."></textarea>
        </label>
      </section>

      <div class="location-brief-contact__grid">
        <label>
          <span>Name</span>
          <input type="text" name="name" autocomplete="name" required>
        </label>
        <label>
          <span>Email</span>
          <input type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required>
        </label>
        <label>
          <span>Company <em>optional</em></span>
          <input type="text" name="company" autocomplete="organization">
        </label>
        <label>
          <span>Phone <em>optional</em></span>
          <input type="tel" name="phone" autocomplete="tel">
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="location-brief-contact__actions">
        <button class="recommendations-button" type="submit" data-location-brief-submit-button>Request Expert Review</button>
        <p data-location-brief-contact-status></p>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<script id="location-knowledge-graph-data" type="application/json">{{ locationKnowledgeGraph | dump | safe }}</script>
<script id="recommendation-profiles-data" type="application/json">{{ recommendationProfiles | dump | safe }}</script>
<script id="recommendation-representative-buildings-data" type="application/json">{{ recommendationRepresentativeBuildings | dump | safe }}</script>
<script src="/js/recommendation-resolver.js" defer></script>
<script src="/js/recommendation-representative-buildings.js" defer></script>
<script src="/js/recommendation-context.js" defer></script>
